00:23:58.080 --> 00:24:00.090
So let's talk a little bit about

00:24:01.650 --> 00:24:06.520
the difference between adult addiction

00:24:06.520 --> 00:24:11.410
and what is unique about teens and substance abuse.

00:24:11.410 --> 00:24:14.200
And maybe that's an opening to talk about

00:24:14.200 --> 00:24:15.400
the developing mind,

00:24:15.400 --> 00:24:17.880
and, you know, what's particular

00:24:17.880 --> 00:24:21.723
about a young person's experiences with drugs and alcohol.

00:24:23.000 --> 00:24:27.863
Adolescents from about puberty to the early 20s

00:24:28.940 --> 00:24:33.170
are in this period of unmatched brain plasticity.

00:24:33.170 --> 00:24:35.840
The only time where the brain is developing at this rate

00:24:35.840 --> 00:24:37.580
is from birth to two.

00:24:37.580 --> 00:24:41.290
So adolescence is so much is happening in their brains.

00:24:41.290 --> 00:24:45.240
They're not only wiring up the frontal lobe of their brain

00:24:45.240 --> 00:24:47.300
that hasn't been really online yet,

00:24:47.300 --> 00:24:50.120
which is where all that executive function, planning,

00:24:50.120 --> 00:24:51.889
schedules, all that stuff happens.

00:24:51.889 --> 00:24:55.430
They're sort of limbic system, lower brain stuff

00:24:55.430 --> 00:24:58.470
is sort of running the show right now.

00:24:58.470 --> 00:25:01.332
This is just starting to come online.

00:25:01.332 --> 00:25:04.080
Myelination is happening in the brain.

00:25:04.080 --> 00:25:07.531
Fatty sheath is going over the neurons, synaptogenesis.

00:25:07.531 --> 00:25:11.560
Synopsis or just billions of synopsis are happening.

00:25:11.560 --> 00:25:16.440
And there's no retakes on this, right?

00:25:16.440 --> 00:25:20.220
So if we get, if anything goes wrong during this period,

00:25:20.220 --> 00:25:23.460
this period of incredible plasticity,

00:25:23.460 --> 00:25:25.900
can't go back and fix it.

00:25:25.900 --> 00:25:28.350
And that's why during adolescents,

00:25:28.350 --> 00:25:31.510
drugs and alcohol do some things to the brain

00:25:31.510 --> 00:25:35.060
that just don't happen later.

00:25:35.060 --> 00:25:38.240
Like there are risks to certain drugs and alcohol,

00:25:38.240 --> 00:25:41.560
to everyone, but then there are greater risks

00:25:41.560 --> 00:25:44.170
for many of them because they mess with parts of the brain

00:25:44.170 --> 00:25:46.240
that are in the process of growing

00:25:46.240 --> 00:25:49.540
and adapting and connecting really, really quickly.

00:25:49.540 --> 00:25:52.575
So that's what makes it different.

00:25:52.575 --> 00:25:56.540
And then, you know, a lot of people call a substance abuse

00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:57.690
a developmental disorder

00:25:57.690 --> 00:26:00.570
because teenagers are also uniquely wired

00:26:00.570 --> 00:26:02.400
to wanna go there, right?

00:26:02.400 --> 00:26:04.120
Novelty, risk.

00:26:04.120 --> 00:26:09.120
Kids, adolescents have baseline lower levels of dopamine

00:26:09.120 --> 00:26:10.700
than little kids or adults.

00:26:10.700 --> 00:26:12.904
So when teenagers tell you they're bored,

